    "narrative": "The lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP today leans heavily into efficiency against the Scherzer and Lugo matchups, with **Brice Turang** anchoring the top of the order as our premier play. Boasting a score of 67.64, **Brice Turang** benefits from a coveted leadoff spot against Rocker, providing a +10% boost that makes him our primary engine for Runs and the critical SB category. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (66.80) and **Jose Caballero** (64.72) are locked in as elite OF options; both are taking full advantage of dynamic platoon edges (+14% and +13% respectively), which effectively weaponizes their speed against arms that struggle to contain the running game.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the board was the exclusion of **Isaac Paredes**, whose 52.86 score fell just short of the 60+ threshold. While **Isaac Paredes** saw a nice boost from favorable wind conditions and a strong spot in the three-hole, the raw projected efficiency of **Trevor Story** and **Cole Young** in the middle infield slots ultimately held firm. Despite the lower batting order for **Trevor Story**, his matchup against Warren presents a higher cumulative floor. We are keeping a close eye on **Seiya Suzuki**; while his 52.47 score is buoyed by his #2 spot in the lineup, he faces the toughest arm of the day in Burns (3.45 xERA), making his performance a high-risk variable for our daily total. \n\nRisk management remains the priority as we navigate this stretch of the season. We have benched **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Edwin Arroyo** to preserve our game caps, as their sub-45 scores against tough LHP assignments like Messick and Imanaga simply didn't justify the roster spot today. With the offense constructed to maximize speed through **Brice Turang**, **Jose Caballero**, and the rest of our lineup, we are well-positioned to squeeze out efficiency in the SB category without over-extending our exposure to the tougher pitchers on the slate.",
